  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "The Lumberjack look is defined by a specific set of garments, materials, and grooming choices that create a rugged and masculine silhouette.",
    "Clothing": "The most iconic garment of the aesthetic is the flannel shirt, particularly in a red-and-black buffalo plaid pattern. This is typically paired with durable trousers, such as raw or selvedge denim jeans or duck canvas work pants. Outerwear consists of functional pieces like chore coats, denim trucker jackets, or down-filled vests. The emphasis is on sturdy, natural fabrics like wool, denim, and canvas.",
    "Footwear and Accessories": "Essential to the look is a pair of heavy-duty work boots. Brands like Timberland and Red Wing are iconic to the style, valued for their durability and classic design. Common accessories include a beanie (or \"watch cap\"), thick wool socks, and leather belts.",
    "Grooming": "The defining grooming characteristic of the Lumberjack aesthetic is the full beard. The rise of the \"lumbersexual\" is directly credited with bringing beards back into mainstream fashion for men after decades of being out of favor. Hair is often worn longer and less styled."
  },
